    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `telephoneDisplay` field \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec by the openapi-generator plugin), documenting the \"country code, space, national digits grouped in threes\" format.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a static `telephoneDisplay(String)` method (the single source of truth for the transform) plus a `groupDigits` helper. It splits the country code using the existing `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` table (longest-prefix-first, so `+61` and `+1` are recognized), then groups the national digits left-to-right in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. A `null` stays `null`; a non-E.164 string is returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` with a `formatTelephoneDisplay(owner)` default method delegating to `Owner.telephoneDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`, matching the established pattern for the other derived read-only fields.\n\nThe target test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (asserting `telephone` = `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`) and the full suite pass.",
