        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots into the existing structure cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** The display transform lives in `Owner` as a static alongside `normalizeTelephone` and the `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` table \u2014 the same place every other derived value (`householdId`, `locality`, `checkDigit`, `ageBand`, \u2026) already lives. The mapper's `formatTelephoneDisplay(owner)` is a verbatim match for the established delegation pattern (null-guard, then delegate to `Owner.<x>(...)`), so a maintainer would find it exactly where they'd expect.\n\n- **Good reuse, no new catch-all.** Country-code identification reuses the existing `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` table rather than introducing a parallel list, and `groupDigits` is an appropriately small, single-purpose private helper. `Owner` is already the home for this family of statics, so adding one more is additive, not bloating.\n\n- **Consistent surface.** The OpenAPI `telephoneDisplay` entry mirrors the title/description/`readOnly` shape of the sibling fields, and the `@Mapping` line sits with its peers.\n\nMinor, not blocking: `telephoneDisplay` and `hasValidNationalNumberLength` both do a longest-prefix scan of `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` (`digits.startsWith(countryCode)`), so there's a small structural echo of the prefix-match loop. They serve different purposes and neither is complex, so factoring out a shared \"find matching country code\" helper would be optional polish, not a structural problem."
